      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Relative Entropy Variational, Chain, and Conditioning Rules",
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $P,Q$ be probability measures on one measurable space and use $D(P\\Vert Q)$ as defined in [[def-tdmath-finite-region-relative-entropy]]. Then\n$$D(P\\Vert Q)=\\sup_{\\phi\\in B_b}\\left(P(\\phi)-\\log Q(e^\\phi)\\right),$$\nwhere $B_b$ is the set of bounded real measurable functions. In particular $D\\geq0$. If $T$ is measurable, then $D(P\\circ T^{-1}\\Vert Q\\circ T^{-1})\\leq D(P\\Vert Q)$.\n\nFor standard-Borel spaces $X,Y$, probability reference measures $Q_X,Q_Y$, and a joint probability $P_{XY}\\ll Q_X\\otimes Q_Y$ with finite $D(P_{XY}\\Vert Q_X\\otimes Q_Y)$, let $P_{Y|X=x}$ be the conditional law supplied by [[thm-conditional-density-formula]]. Then\n$$D(P_{XY}\\Vert Q_X\\otimes Q_Y)=D(P_X\\Vert Q_X)+\\int_X D(P_{Y|X=x}\\Vert Q_Y)\\,P_X(dx).$$\nMore generally, for random variables $R,S,Y$ taking values in standard-Borel spaces $\\mathcal R,\\mathcal S,\\mathcal Y$, with $R=r(S)$ for a measurable $r:\\mathcal S\\to\\mathcal R$, and a probability reference $Q_Y$ on $\\mathcal Y$, the conditional increments\n$$G(R):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|R}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right],\\qquad G(S):=E_P\\!\\left[D(P_{Y|S}\\Vert Q_Y)\\right]$$\nsatisfy $0\\leq G(R)\\leq G(S)$ whenever $D(P_{S,Y}\\Vert P_S\\otimes Q_Y)<\\infty$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-tdmath-finite-region-relative-entropy",
          "def-standard-borel-space",
          "thm-radon-nikodym-density-exists-and-is-unique-up-to-almost-everywhere-equality",
