      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-poisson-reference-count-properties",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Poisson Reference Counts and Translation Invariance",
        "statement": "Assume AC, fix $d\\geq1$ and $\\lambda>0$, and let $Q_\\lambda$ be the configuration law of [[def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference]]. Define the intensity measure on Borel sets by $\\Lambda_{Q_\\lambda}(A):=E_{Q_\\lambda}N_A$, where $N_A=\\omega(A)$ and the nonnegative expectation may be infinite. For pairwise disjoint bounded Borel sets $A_1,\\ldots,A_r\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$, the restrictions $\\omega|_{A_1},\\ldots,\\omega|_{A_r}$ are independent, each count $N_{A_j}$ has Poisson law with mean $\\lambda|A_j|$, and the joint law of counts on any finite disjoint family is the product of those Poisson laws. In particular, $Q_\\lambda$ is invariant under every translation $T_x$, and $\\Lambda_{Q_\\lambda}(A)=\\lambda|A|$ for every Borel $A$. For every bounded Borel $A$ and real $a$, its count also has the exact exponential moment\n$$E_{Q_\\lambda}e^{aN_A}=\\exp\\!\\left(\\lambda|A|(e^a-1)\\right).$$",
        "deps": [
          "def-real-exponential-function-and-e",
          "thm-monotone-convergence-for-the-integral",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference",
          "lem-tdmath-counts-generate-configuration-sigma",
          "def-multinomial-coefficient",
          "thm-multinomial-theorem",
          "thm-exponential-addition-formula",
