      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-specific-entropy-density",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Specific Relative Entropy Density",
        "statement": "Assume AC and let $P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}(\\Omega)$, with this class defined in [[def-tdmath-local-tame-topology]], be stationary for the translations of [[def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference]]. For a bounded Borel set $G$, write $P_G$ and $Q_G$ for the restrictions of $P$ and the unit-intensity Poisson reference $Q$ to configurations in $G$. For $L>0$, put $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$ and\n$$D_L:=D(P_{\\Lambda_L}\\Vert Q_{\\Lambda_L}).$$\nThen the specific relative entropy density\n$$I(P):=\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}\\frac{D_L}{L^d}$$\nexists in $[0,+\\infty]$ and satisfies\n$$I(P)=\\sup_{m\\in\\mathbb N,\\ m\\geq1}\\frac{D(P_{\\Lambda_m}\\Vert Q_{\\Lambda_m})}{m^d}.$$\nIf $I(P)<\\infty$, every bounded Borel restriction has finite relative entropy. This is an information functional relative to the specified unit-intensity Poisson law; changing the reference changes its value.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference",
          "thm-tdmath-poisson-reference-count-properties",
          "def-tdmath-finite-region-relative-entropy",
          "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
          "def-tdmath-local-tame-topology"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
