      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-conditional-log-density-convergence",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Conditional Log-Density Convergence for the Poisson Reference",
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}(\\Omega)$, as defined in [[def-tdmath-local-tame-topology]], have finite specific relative entropy $I(P)=\\gamma<\\infty$ relative to the unit-intensity reference $Q$ of [[def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference]]. Let $C=[0,1)^d$ be the reference cell and order the other unit cells lexicographically; $F_+$ is the set of cells preceding $C$. For each finite $A\\subset F_+$ let $k_A$ be the conditional density of the configuration in $C$ given the configuration in $A$, relative to $Q_C$, as supplied by [[thm-conditional-density-formula]]. Then\n$$g(A):=E_P[\\log k_A]=D(P_{A\\cup C}\\Vert Q_{A\\cup C})-D(P_A\\Vert Q_A)$$\nis finite, nonnegative, and increasing with finite $A$, with $\\sup\\{g(A):A\\subset F_+\\text{ finite}\\}=\\gamma$. For any increasing finite exhaustion $A_m\\uparrow F_+$, the densities $k_{A_m}$ converge in $L^1(P_{F_+}\\otimes Q_C)$ to a density $k_\\infty$ of $P_{F_+\\cup C}$ relative to $P_{F_+}\\otimes Q_C$, and\n$$\\log k_{A_m}\\longrightarrow\\log k_\\infty\\quad\\text{in }L^1(P).$$\nThe logarithmic convergence is directed: for every $\\varepsilon>0$ some finite $A_m$ satisfies $\\sup_{B\\supseteq A_m,\\ B\\subset F_+\\text{ finite}}E_P|\\log k_B-\\log k_\\infty|<\\varepsilon$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-tdmath-poisson-configuration-reference",
          "thm-tdmath-poisson-reference-count-properties",
          "def-tdmath-finite-region-relative-entropy",
          "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
