      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Compactness of Finite-Specific-Entropy Levels in the Local-Tame Topology",
        "statement": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB. Let\n$$\\mathcal H_c:=\\{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}(\\Omega): I(P)\\leq c\\},\\qquad c\\in[0,\\infty),$$\nwhere $I$ and the local-tame topology $\\tau_L$ are defined by [[thm-tdmath-specific-entropy-density]] and [[def-tdmath-local-tame-topology]]. Then $\\mathcal H_c$ is compact and sequentially compact in $\\tau_L$. This is a pure measure-theoretic compactness theorem for simple locally finite configurations relative to the independent unit-intensity Poisson reference; it makes no thermodynamic-limit or physical claim.",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-ultrafilter-extension-principle",
          "def-dependent-choice",
          "def-hahn-banach-extension-principle-relative",
